IMPORT prelude

-- Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990 (Singapore) -- employing a foreigner without a valid work pass and its penalties (s 5),
-- the occupier of a construction work place (s 6A), terminating on revocation (s 9), self-employed foreigners (s 10), when the levy
-- stops and the cap on late-payment penalty (s 11), what a work pass covers (s 12), kickbacks and phantom passes (ss 22A, 22B,
-- 23A), the costs the employer must bear and the financial penalties the Controller may impose (s 25), appeals (s 25G), and
-- composition (s 27).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EFMA1990.txt ("version in
-- force from 1/12/2025"), with amendments to Act 31 of 2023 (wef 1 December 2025) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the duties and penalties an employer,
-- a foreign worker or a principal contractor actually meets. Not encoded: appointments (s 3), the Controller's application and
-- debarment powers (s 7), the register (s 8), custody and loss of passes (ss 13, 14), inspection, arrest and
-- service powers (ss 16 to 21G), the general offences in s 22 beyond their maxima, prescribed-infringement procedure
-- (ss 25B to 25F, 25H), regulations (s 29), the levy rates themselves (set by order, not in the Act), and the Schedule.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990 -- work passes`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2, 5 -- employing a foreign employee without a valid work pass`

-- s 2: "foreigner" means "any person who is not a citizen of Singapore or permanent resident of Singapore"; "foreign employee"
-- means "any foreigner, other than a self-employed foreigner, who seeks or is offered employment in Singapore". "employ" covers
-- any work or training "whether under a contract of service or otherwise, and with or without salary".
-- s 5(1): "A person must not employ a foreign employee unless the foreign employee has a valid work pass." (3): nor "otherwise than
-- in accordance with the conditions of the foreign employee's work pass".
DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore citizen`
    `a permanent resident`
    `a foreigner`

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Status, `has a valid work pass` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employing the worker contravenes s 5(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the worker`
    WHEN `a foreigner` THEN NOT `has a valid work pass`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 5(4): not knowing the employee was a foreigner is NOT a defence "unless the defendant further proves that the defendant had
-- exercised due diligence to ascertain the nationality of the employee". (5): no due diligence "unless the defendant had checked the
-- passport, document of identity or other travel document of the employee". Checking the document is necessary; the text does
-- not say it is sufficient, so both are asked.
GIVEN `did not know the worker was a foreigner` IS A BOOLEAN, `exercised due diligence on nationality` IS A BOOLEAN, `checked the passport or identity document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ignorance defence to s 5(1) succeeds` IF
    `did not know the worker was a foreigner` AND `exercised due diligence on nationality` AND `checked the passport or identity document`

-- s 5(6)(a): first conviction -- "a fine of at least $5,000 and not more than $30,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 12 months or to both". (b) second or subsequent: (i) individual -- fine $10,000 to $30,000 "and with imprisonment for a term of
-- not less than one month and not more than 12 months"; (ii) any other case -- fine $20,000 to $60,000 (no imprisonment).
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5(6) minimum fine` MEANS
    IF NOT `is a repeat conviction` THEN 5000
    ELSE IF `is an individual` THEN 10000 ELSE 20000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5(6) maximum fine` MEANS
    IF NOT `is a repeat conviction` THEN 30000
    ELSE IF `is an individual` THEN 30000 ELSE 60000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5(6) minimum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat conviction` AND `is an individual` THEN 1 ELSE 0

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5(6) maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF NOT `is a repeat conviction` THEN 12
    ELSE IF `is an individual` THEN 12 ELSE 0

-- s 5(9): (a) a prior conviction under s 5(1) of the old Employment of Foreign Workers Act counts; (b) "all convictions against the
-- same person for the contravention of subsection (1) at one and the same trial shall be deemed to be one conviction".
GIVEN `convicted under s 5(1) at an earlier trial` IS A BOOLEAN, `convicted under the old Act s 5(1) before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this is a second or subsequent s 5(6) conviction` IF
    `convicted under s 5(1) at an earlier trial` OR `convicted under the old Act s 5(1) before`

§§ `6, 6A -- presumptions against the occupier`

-- s 6: "Where a foreigner is found at any premises, the occupier of the premises is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have
-- employed the foreigner."
-- s 6A(1): an occupier of a work place with control of access "must not permit any foreigner without a valid work pass to enter or
-- remain at the work place". (7): "occupier" means "the principal contractor who undertakes any construction works at the work
-- place" (and anyone the Minister specifies). (2): control, permission and knowledge are all presumed. (3): ignorance does not
-- rebut "unless the defendant further proves that the defendant had exercised due diligence -- (a) to prevent the foreigner from
-- entering or remaining ...; (b) to ascertain that the person was a citizen ... or permanent resident ... by checking the person's
-- passport ...; or (c) to ascertain that the foreigner had ... a valid work pass by checking his or her original work pass".
-- INFERENCE: the "or" is read as making (a), (b), (c) alternatives; any one suffices. (4): due diligence under (a) needs "all
-- reasonable measures ... including all the measures prescribed".
GIVEN `did not know the person was a foreigner` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable and prescribed measures to keep them out` IS A BOOLEAN, `checked their passport` IS A BOOLEAN, `checked their original work pass` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 6A presumptions are rebutted by ignorance` IF
    `did not know the person was a foreigner`
    AND (`took all reasonable and prescribed measures to keep them out` OR `checked their passport` OR `checked their original work pass`)

GIVEN `is the principal contractor for construction works there` IS A BOOLEAN, `is specified by the Minister as occupier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an occupier for s 6A` IF
    `is the principal contractor for construction works there` OR `is specified by the Minister as occupier`

-- s 6A(6): (a) fine not exceeding $15,000 or 12 months or both; (b) second or subsequent -- $30,000 or 2 years or both.
GIVEN `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 6A maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 30000 ELSE 15000

GIVEN `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 6A maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 24 ELSE 12

§§ `9 -- termination when the pass is suspended or revoked`

-- s 9(1): on notification of a suspension or revocation, the employer "must, within 7 days of receiving the notification,
-- terminate the employment". (3): the Controller may impose "a financial penalty of an amount, not exceeding $10,000" -- a
-- prescribed infringement (s 2), not an offence. (6): the employee is not "deemed to be employed under an illegal contract of
-- employment" by reason only of the contravention.
GIVEN `days from notification to termination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer complied with s 9(1)` IF
    `days from notification to termination` AT MOST 7

§§ `10 -- self-employed foreigners`

-- s 10(1): "A foreigner must not be a self-employed foreigner unless he or she has a valid work pass." (2)(a): fine up to $20,000 or
-- 2 years or both; (b) second or subsequent: "imprisonment for a term of not less than one month and not more than 2 years and also
-- be liable to a fine not exceeding $20,000".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Status, `works on own account in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a valid work pass` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes s 10(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a foreigner` THEN `works on own account in Singapore` AND (NOT `has a valid work pass`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 10 minimum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 1 ELSE 0

§§ `11 -- the levy`

-- s 11(2): "The levy continues to be payable unless the work pass -- (a) has expired; (b) has been suspended or revoked by the
-- Controller; or (c) has been cancelled by the Controller on application by the employer." The worker leaving, or the employment
-- ending, is not on the list.
GIVEN `the pass has expired` IS A BOOLEAN, `the pass was suspended or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN, `the pass was cancelled on the employer's application` IS A BOOLEAN, `the worker has stopped working` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the levy is still payable` IF
    NOT (`the pass has expired` OR `the pass was suspended or revoked` OR `the pass was cancelled on the employer's application`)

-- s 11(4): late levy attracts a penalty "for every day the amount remains unpaid", at a rate set by order; (5): "the total penalty
-- must not exceed 30% of the amount of levy outstanding".
GIVEN `penalty at the ordered rate` IS A NUMBER, `levy outstanding` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the levy late-payment penalty` MEANS
    `the lower of` `penalty at the ordered rate` (`levy outstanding` TIMES 30 DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `12 -- what a work pass covers`

-- s 12(1): a pass for a foreign employee "is valid only in respect of the employer and the foreign employee specified in the work
-- pass", and the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified (or submitted in the application), or any other for
-- which the employee "has the Controller's approval". (3): valid for the period specified unless earlier suspended, revoked or
-- cancelled.
GIVEN `for the employer named in the pass` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the occupation specified or submitted` IS A BOOLEAN, `in an occupation the Controller approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the pass period` IS A BOOLEAN, `suspended, revoked or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pass covers the work` IF
        `for the employer named in the pass`
    AND (`in the occupation specified or submitted` OR `in an occupation the Controller approved`)
    AND `within the pass period`
    AND (NOT `suspended, revoked or cancelled`)

§§ `22A, 25(4), 25(6) -- money taken from the worker`

-- s 22A(1): no one may deduct from salary, or "demand or receive, directly or indirectly and whether in Singapore or elsewhere",
-- any sum (a) as consideration or a condition for employment, (b) for continued employment, or (c) "as a financial guarantee
-- related, in any way, to the employment". (2): fine up to $30,000 or 2 years or both. (3): any other sum is "presumed, until the
-- contrary is proved," to be consideration for the employment, unless it is (a) a charge the employer must bear under s 25(6),
-- (b) a fee prescribed as recoverable from the employee, (c)/(d) a deduction authorised by the Employment Act 1968 ss 26 to 32 or
-- the terms of employment, or (e) a fee an Employment Agencies Act licensee may lawfully charge.
-- s 25(6): the employer, "except where the Controller permits otherwise", must bear (a) work pass fees; (b) security costs;
-- (c) medical insurance; (d) medical examinations; (e) the levy and penalty; (f) training "required by the employer or the
-- Controller"; (g) repatriation "at any time"; (h) anything prescribed. s 25(4): recovering any of these from the worker -- a
-- financial penalty up to $20,000.
DECLARE Charge IS ONE OF
    `a fee for getting the job`
    `a fee for keeping the job`
    `a security deposit from the worker`
    `the foreign worker levy`
    `work pass application fees`
    `medical insurance premiums`
    `medical examination costs`
    `repatriation costs`
    `employer-required training costs`
    `an Employment Act authorised deduction`
    `a lawful employment agency fee`
    `an unexplained deduction`

GIVEN `the charge` IS A Charge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must bear the charge` IF
    CONSIDER `the charge`
    WHEN `the foreign worker levy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `work pass application fees` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `medical insurance premiums` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `medical examination costs` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `repatriation costs` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `employer-required training costs` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the charge` IS A Charge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking the charge falls squarely within s 22A(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the charge`
    WHEN `a fee for getting the job` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a fee for keeping the job` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a security deposit from the worker` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the charge` IS A Charge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking the charge is presumed a kickback under s 22A(3)` IF
        (NOT `the employer must bear the charge` `the charge`)
    AND CONSIDER `the charge`
        WHEN `an Employment Act authorised deduction` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a lawful employment agency fee` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the charge` IS A Charge, `the presumption is rebutted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking the charge is an offence under s 22A(2)` IF
        `taking the charge falls squarely within s 22A(1)` `the charge`
    OR  (`taking the charge is presumed a kickback under s 22A(3)` `the charge` AND (NOT `the presumption is rebutted`))

GIVEN `the charge` IS A Charge, `the Controller permitted otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is exposed to a s 25(4) financial penalty` IF
    `the employer must bear the charge` `the charge` AND (NOT `the Controller permitted otherwise`)

-- s 23A(1)(a): on conviction under s 22A(2) the court "shall, in addition to imposing ... any other punishment, order the person to
-- pay" a sum "equal to the amount of the sum or other benefit ... the person deducted or received".
GIVEN `amount taken from the worker` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 23A payment order` MEANS `amount taken from the worker`

§§ `22B -- phantom work passes`

-- s 22B(1): obtaining a work pass "for a trade or business that does not exist, that is not in operation or that does not require
-- the employment of such a foreign employee" AND failing to employ the foreign employee -- "imprisonment for a presumptive minimum
-- term of not less than 6 months and not more than 2 years" and a fine up to $6,000.
-- (2): "charged with more than 5 offences" and "convicted of at least 6 of those offences at the same trial" -- caning in addition,
-- subject to CPC ss 325(1) and 330(1); (3) a person not punishable with caning gets a fine up to $10,000 in lieu.
GIVEN `the business does not exist, is not operating or does not need the worker` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to employ the worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obtaining the pass is a s 22B(1) offence` IF
    `the business does not exist, is not operating or does not need the worker` AND `failed to employ the worker`

GIVEN `offences charged` IS A NUMBER, `offences convicted at the same trial` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `caning is mandated under s 22B(2)` IF
    `offences charged` GREATER THAN 5 AND `offences convicted at the same trial` AT LEAST 6

§§ `25 -- maximum financial penalties for prescribed infringements`

-- s 25(1): inflating the employer's foreign employee entitlement -- not exceeding $20,000. (2): breaching a regulatory condition --
-- $10,000. (3): an employer who "inadvertently, or without intent to mislead or defraud," gives inaccurate information -- $20,000.
-- (4): recovering s 25(6) costs from the worker -- $20,000. s 9(3): not terminating within 7 days -- $10,000. s 25A(2): breaching a
-- prescribed duty after in-principle approval -- $10,000.
-- Contrast s 22(1)(d): a statement the person "knows, or ought reasonably to know, is false" is an OFFENCE -- fine up to $20,000 or
-- 2 years or both.
DECLARE Infringement IS ONE OF
    `inflating the foreign employee entitlement`
    `breaching a regulatory condition`
    `inadvertently giving inaccurate information`
    `recovering employer-borne costs from the worker`
    `not terminating within 7 days of revocation`
    `breaching a prescribed duty`

GIVEN `the infringement` IS A Infringement
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum financial penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the infringement`
    WHEN `inflating the foreign employee entitlement` THEN 20000
    WHEN `breaching a regulatory condition` THEN 10000
    WHEN `inadvertently giving inaccurate information` THEN 20000
    WHEN `recovering employer-borne costs from the worker` THEN 20000
    WHEN `not terminating within 7 days of revocation` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 10000

§§ `25G -- appeals to the Appeal Board`

-- s 25G(1): an appeal "must be lodged within 14 days after the receipt of the determination or direction". (3): an appeal "does
-- not suspend the effect of the determination or direction ... unless the appeal is against the imposition, or the amount, of a
-- financial penalty".
GIVEN `days after receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days after receipt` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `the appeal is against the imposition or amount of a financial penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal suspends the determination` IF
    `the appeal is against the imposition or amount of a financial penalty`

§§ `27 -- composition`

-- s 27(1): the Controller may compound any offence by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of
-- the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) a sum of $5,000."
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
